IMPORT prelude

-- Financial Holding Companies Act 2013 (Singapore) -- what a financial holding company is and which can be designated (ss 2(1), 4),
-- holding out and use of the name (ss 6, 7), the activities a designated company may carry on (s 8), the controller thresholds and
-- who must approve a change in shareholding or control (ss 11 to 14, 19 to 21), the penalties and defences for those (s 26), and the
-- limits on major stakes and immovable property (ss 31, 32).
--
-- Edition: Act 13 of 2013, informal consolidation ("version in force from 9/3/2025"), as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/FHCA2013.txt, with amendments to Act 5 of 2025 (wef 9 March 2025) annotated. The deposit is the Act
-- as numbered in 2013 ("No. 13 of 2013"); it is NOT marked as a 2020 Revised Edition text.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Cited by 9 of the 527 Singapore Acts deposited in this repository. SCOPED to the provisions a group, a shareholder or
-- a practitioner meets first: whether a company is caught, the approvals needed to buy into one, and the two hard investment limits.
-- Not encoded: information-gathering (s 3), withdrawal (s 5), levy (s 9), constitution changes (s 10), the Minister's and Authority's
-- objection and direction powers (ss 17, 18, 23, 24, 27), exposures and equity limits (ss 28 to 30, set by regulations), capital and
-- liquidity (Part VI, set by notice), audit and inspection (Part VII), control and winding up (Part VIII), foreign assistance (Part
-- IX), and Part X. "Substantial shareholder" is defined by reference to s 81 of the Companies Act, which was not read: it is an input.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules conventions. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Financial Holding Companies Act 2013 -- control`

§§ `2(1) and 4 -- financial holding companies and designation`

-- s 2(1): "financial holding company" means a holding company (a) "which has at least one subsidiary that is a bank incorporated in
-- Singapore or a licensed insurer incorporated, formed or established in Singapore"; and (b) whose financial-institution subsidiaries
-- "in the aggregate account, for 50% or more of the assets, capital, liabilities or revenue, of the FHC group".
-- Any ONE of the four measures reaching 50% is enough; the input is the largest of the four.
GIVEN `is a holding company` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `has a Singapore bank or licensed insurer subsidiary` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `largest financial share of the group in percent` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a financial holding company` IF
        `is a holding company`
    AND `has a Singapore bank or licensed insurer subsidiary`
    AND `largest financial share of the group in percent` AT LEAST 50

-- s 4(1): the Authority MAY designate (a) "an ultimate financial holding company incorporated, formed or established in Singapore";
-- or (b) an intermediate one incorporated etc. in Singapore whose Singapore bank or licensed insurer subsidiary is considered by the
-- Authority (i) "significant to the FHC group" or (ii) to "affect the stability of, or public confidence in, the financial system".
-- (4): appeal to the Minister within 30 days of the Gazette order; (5) designation continues pending appeal.
DECLARE Tier IS ONE OF
    `ultimate`
    `intermediate`

GIVEN `the tier` IS A Tier,
      `incorporated in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the subsidiary is significant or systemic` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may be designated` IF
        `incorporated in Singapore`
    AND CONSIDER `the tier`
        WHEN `ultimate` THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE `the subsidiary is significant or systemic`

GIVEN `days after the Gazette order` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the designation appeal is in time` IF
    `days after the Gazette order` AT MOST 30

§§ `6 and 7 -- holding out and use of the name`

-- s 6(1): "No person shall hold itself out as a designated financial holding company if it is not designated"; (2) fine up to
-- $100,000, and $10,000 a day continuing.
GIVEN `holds itself out as designated` IS A BOOLEAN, `is designated` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `holding out is an offence` IF
    `holds itself out as designated` AND (NOT `is designated`)

-- s 7(1): no person "other than an excepted person" shall, without the Authority's prior approval, in the course of business, use a
-- name, logo or trade mark indicating association with a designated financial holding company. (4) excepted persons include a
-- related-corporation financial institution, officers and agents, and regulated or incidental businesses under arrangement with the
-- group. (5): a person "lawfully using" the name immediately before the designation date may continue "for a period of 3 years".
-- (3): an individual up to $125,000 ($12,500 a day continuing); any other person up to $250,000 ($25,000 a day).
GIVEN `uses the name in business` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `is an excepted person` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `has the Authority's approval` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `was lawfully using it before designation` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `years since the designation date` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `use of the name is an offence` IF
        `uses the name in business`
    AND (NOT `is an excepted person`)
    AND (NOT `has the Authority's approval`)
    AND (NOT (`was lawfully using it before designation` AND `years since the designation date` AT MOST 3))

GIVEN `is an individual` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine for misusing the name` MEANS
    IF `is an individual` THEN 125000 ELSE 250000

§§ `8 -- activities`

-- s 8(1): a designated financial holding company "shall not carry out any activity without the approval of the Authority, other
-- than" (a) being a holding company for its subsidiaries; (b) holding shares as permitted under s 31; (c) to support the group's
-- business, (i) general, capital and liquidity management and (ii) advisory, financial, accounting or information processing
-- services; (d) activities specified by the Authority by notice. (2): fine up to $250,000.
DECLARE Activity IS ONE OF
    `holding its subsidiaries`
    `holding shares permitted under s 31`
    `capital and liquidity management for the group`
    `accounting services for the group`
    `IT processing for the group`
    `lending to the public`
    `selling insurance to the public`
    `property development`
    `an activity specified by Authority notice`

GIVEN `the activity` IS AN Activity
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the activity needs approval` IF
    CONSIDER `the activity`
    WHEN `lending to the public` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `selling insurance to the public` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `property development` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `11 -- controllers`

-- s 11(2): "20% controller" -- a person who alone or with associates "holds not less than 20%" of the issued shares or "is in a
-- position to control voting power of not less than 20%". "12% controller" -- a person, "not being a 20% controller", at not less
-- than 12% on either measure. Associates (s 11(3)(c)) include family, controlled bodies, subsidiaries and parties acting together.
GIVEN `shares in percent` IS A NUMBER, `votes in percent` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a 20% controller` IF
    `shares in percent` AT LEAST 20 OR `votes in percent` AT LEAST 20

GIVEN `shares in percent` IS A NUMBER, `votes in percent` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a 12% controller` IF
        (NOT (`is a 20% controller` `shares in percent` `votes in percent`))
    AND (`shares in percent` AT LEAST 12 OR `votes in percent` AT LEAST 12)

-- ss 13(3), 20(3), (4): an agreement "to act together" over voting shares "of an aggregate of 5% or more of the total votes".
GIVEN `aggregate votes in percent` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the pact is caught` IF
    `aggregate votes in percent` AT LEAST 5

§§ `12 to 14 and 19 to 21 -- who must approve`

-- With bank subsidiary (a Singapore-incorporated bank in the group): the MINISTER approves a merger or take-over (s 12(1)), becoming
-- a substantial shareholder (s 13(1)), a 5% acting-together pact over "acquisition, holding or disposal" (s 13(3)), and becoming a
-- 12%, 20% or indirect controller (s 14(1)). Approval needs the Authority's fit-and-proper finding AND the Minister's view that it is
-- "in the national interest" (ss 12(2), 15(1)).
-- Without bank subsidiary: the AUTHORITY approves a merger (s 19(1)), becoming a substantial shareholder (s 20(1)), a pact over
-- "acquisition or holding" or voting (s 20(3)), and becoming a 20% or indirect controller (s 21(1)). A pact over DISPOSAL needs only
-- "first notifying the Authority" (s 20(4)). Section 21 has NO 12% controller tier, so becoming a 12% controller of such a company
-- needs nobody's approval under these sections.
DECLARE Step IS ONE OF
    `a merger or take-over`
    `becoming a substantial shareholder`
    `an acquisition or voting pact`
    `a disposal pact`
    `becoming a 12% controller`
    `becoming a 20% controller`
    `becoming an indirect controller`

DECLARE Clearance IS ONE OF
    `approval of the Minister`
    `approval of the Authority`
    `notice to the Authority`
    `none under ss 12 to 21`

GIVEN `the step` IS A Step, `has a bank subsidiary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A Clearance
`the clearance needed` MEANS
    IF `has a bank subsidiary`
    THEN `approval of the Minister`
    ELSE CONSIDER `the step`
         WHEN `a disposal pact` THEN `notice to the Authority`
         WHEN `becoming a 12% controller` THEN `none under ss 12 to 21`
         OTHERWISE `approval of the Authority`

-- ss 15(1), 22(1): the approver may approve if the person is fit and proper and the company will carry on prudently; s 15(1)(b) adds
-- for the bank-subsidiary case that "the Minister is satisfied that it is in the national interest".
GIVEN `has a bank subsidiary` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `fit and proper and prudent` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `in the national interest` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the application may be approved` IF
        `fit and proper and prudent`
    AND (`in the national interest` OR (NOT `has a bank subsidiary`))

-- s 25: an appeal to the Minister from an Authority decision under Part IV "within 30 days after he is notified".
GIVEN `days after notification` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Part IV appeal is in time` IF
    `days after notification` AT MOST 30

§§ `26 -- penalties and defences`

-- s 26(1): contravening ss 12(1), 13(1)-(4), 14(1)(a), 19(1), 20(1)-(5) -- an individual up to $125,000; any other person up to
-- $250,000. FINE ONLY.
-- s 26(2): contravening ss 14(1)(b) or (c), 21(1) or (2) (20% and indirect controllers) -- an individual up to $125,000 "or to
-- imprisonment for a term not exceeding 3 years or to both"; any other person up to $250,000.
-- So becoming a 12% controller without approval carries no prison term, but a 20% or indirect controller does.
GIVEN `the step` IS A Step, `is an individual` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum prison term in years` MEANS
    IF `is an individual`
    THEN CONSIDER `the step`
         WHEN `becoming a 20% controller` THEN 3
         WHEN `becoming an indirect controller` THEN 3
         OTHERWISE 0
    ELSE 0

GIVEN `is an individual` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum Part IV fine` MEANS
    IF `is an individual` THEN 125000 ELSE 250000

-- s 26(3): for a contravention of s 13, 14, 20 or 21, a defence to prove (a) "he was not aware that he had contravened" and (b)
-- "within 14 days after becoming aware" he notified the Minister or Authority and took the action directed.
-- s 26(4): for s 14 or 21 only, a further defence even if aware: (a) the contravention resulted from an increase in the holding of a
-- FAMILY associate (s 11(3)(c)(i)); (b) no agreement with that associate; (c) notification "within 14 days of the date of the
-- contravention" and the directed action taken.
-- s 26(5): "Except as provided", lack of intent or knowledge is no defence. Mergers (ss 12, 19) are outside both defences.
GIVEN `the step` IS A Step
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the unawareness defence can apply` IF
    CONSIDER `the step`
    WHEN `a merger or take-over` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the step` IS A Step
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the associate defence can apply` IF
    CONSIDER `the step`
    WHEN `becoming a 12% controller` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `becoming a 20% controller` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `becoming an indirect controller` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the step` IS A Step,
      `was unaware` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `days from awareness to notice` IS A NUMBER,
      `took the directed action` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `has the unawareness defence` IF
        `the unawareness defence can apply` `the step`
    AND `was unaware`
    AND `days from awareness to notice` AT MOST 14
    AND `took the directed action`

GIVEN `the step` IS A Step,
      `caused by a family associate's increase` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `had no pact with that associate` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `days from contravention to notice` IS A NUMBER,
      `took the directed action` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `has the associate defence` IF
        `the associate defence can apply` `the step`
    AND `caused by a family associate's increase`
    AND `had no pact with that associate`
    AND `days from contravention to notice` AT MOST 14
    AND `took the directed action`

§§ `31 and 32 -- major stakes and immovable property`

-- s 31(10): "major stake" -- a beneficial interest "exceeding 10%" of the issued shares, control over "more than 10%" of the voting
-- power, or an interest where the company's directors act on the holding company's directions or it can determine its policy.
-- (1): no designated company shall acquire or hold a major stake "without the prior approval of the Authority"; (2) except "within
-- 6 months after its designation date or such longer period as the Authority may allow"; (7) not security interests in the ordinary
-- course or shares taken in satisfaction of debts "disposed of at the earliest suitable opportunity". (9): up to $250,000.
-- Note the asymmetry with s 11: 12% and 20% are "not less than"; 10% here must be EXCEEDED.
GIVEN `shares in percent` IS A NUMBER, `votes in percent` IS A NUMBER, `directs the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a major stake` IF
    `shares in percent` GREATER THAN 10 OR `votes in percent` GREATER THAN 10 OR `directs the company`

GIVEN `extension in months` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the grace period in months` MEANS
    IF `extension in months` GREATER THAN 6 THEN `extension in months` ELSE 6

GIVEN `shares in percent` IS A NUMBER,
      `votes in percent` IS A NUMBER,
      `directs the company` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `held as security or for a debt` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `months since designation` IS A NUMBER,
      `extension in months` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the stake needs Authority approval` IF
        `is a major stake` `shares in percent` `votes in percent` `directs the company`
    AND (NOT `held as security or for a debt`)
    AND `months since designation` GREATER THAN `the grace period in months` `extension in months`

-- s 32(1): "No designated financial holding company shall acquire or hold interests in or rights over immovable property, wherever
-- situated." (2) the same 6-month grace, after which Authority approval is needed. (5) "immovable property" excludes property used
-- for the group's business or housing or amenities for officers, property held as security or on its enforcement (disposed of at the
-- earliest suitable opportunity), and property held for others under an obligation. (7): up to $100,000.
DECLARE Holding IS ONE OF
    `the group's own office premises`
    `staff housing`
    `property held as loan security`
    `property taken on enforcing security`
    `property held on trust for others`
    `an investment property`
    `vacant land held for capital gain`

GIVEN `the holding` IS A Holding
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is caught by s 32` IF
    CONSIDER `the holding`
    WHEN `an investment property` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `vacant land held for capital gain` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the holding` IS A Holding,
      `months since designation` IS A NUMBER,
      `extension in months` IS A NUMBER,
      `has Authority approval` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `holding the property is an offence` IF
        `is caught by s 32` `the holding`
    AND `months since designation` GREATER THAN `the grace period in months` `extension in months`
    AND (NOT `has Authority approval`)
